# Code owners — Mass AI Atlas
#
# Today the atlas has one maintainer, so everything routes to @holzerjm. That makes
# review requests automatic; it does not by itself block anything.
#
# ⚠️  Do NOT turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in the `main` ruleset while this
# file names a single person. GitHub never counts an author's approval of their own PR
# and the ruleset has no bypass list, so the only maintainer could no longer merge
# anything.
#
# Planned two-person rule, once a second owner exists (a team with at least two members,
# replacing @holzerjm below):
#
#   - The narrative and data files — the founder-stage tips in data/stages.yml,
#     user-visible copy in index.html, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, MAINTAINING.md and
#     docs/ — are approved by someone other than the person who wrote the change, so no
#     one person can reword the project's own framing alone.
#   - CODEOWNERS matches files, not lines, so assigning data/entities.yml to the team
#     means every maintainer-authored data change gets a second reviewer. Community PRs
#     are unaffected in practice: the author is not a maintainer, so one maintainer
#     approval is already a second person. If that proves too heavy for routine rota
#     updates, narrow it with a CI check rather than dropping the rule.
#   - .github/ (the workflows and this file) stays with the owners team, so the rule
#     cannot be edited away by the same person it constrains.
#
# Syntax: the last matching pattern wins; owners need write access to the repo, or the
# line is ignored.
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

